Visentrix Plugin License (VPL)
================================
Version 1.0 — August 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 Visentrix

Layer 3 — Plugins (Hybrid)

This license governs plugins developed for the OSINT Sentinel Workstation.
Plugins are extensions that connect to the Visentrix Open Cockpit (Layer 1)
to add functionality. They may be open source, commercial, private, or
experimental.

WHAT IS A PLUGIN
----------------

A plugin is any software module that:

  - Registers with the workstation's plugin manager via the
    EarthEnginePlugin lifecycle (register, unregister, update,
    getStats, getControls, onControl).
  - Links to the Cockpit layer (Layer 1) through the public plugin API.
  - Does not directly call, import, or link to Core Engine (Layer 2)
    internal modules, kernels, or worker scripts.

PERMITTED USES
--------------

You may:

  a. Develop and distribute open-source plugins under any OSI-approved
     license (MIT, Apache-2.0, GPL, etc.).

  b. Develop and distribute commercial plugins, provided they link only
     to the Cockpit layer (Layer 1) public API.

  c. Develop private or internal plugins for personal or organizational
     use.

  d. Develop mission-specific or experimental plugins.

  e. Sell plugins independently of the Core Engine.

  f. Distribute plugins through any channel (GitHub, marketplace, direct).

RESTRICTIONS
------------

You may NOT:

  a. Develop plugins that directly import, call, or link to Core Engine
     (Layer 2) internal modules. Plugins must use the public Cockpit API
     only.

  b. Develop plugins that bypass or circumvent the license validation,
     machine fingerprinting, or feature gating of the Core Engine.

  c. Develop plugins that extract, replicate, or substitute for the
     Core Engine's compute functionality (HAL, GPU kernels, worker pool,
     streaming I/O, prediction engine, native bridges).

  d. Distribute plugins that include or bundle Core Engine code.

  e. Use the plugin system to create a competing "engine" product that
     replicates the Core Engine's functionality.

CLARIFICATION
-------------

If a plugin needs heavy compute (DEM analysis, band math, anomaly
detection, etc.), it must request that compute through the Cockpit's
public IPC API, which will route the request to the Core Engine if a
valid license is present. The plugin itself must not implement or
replicate the Core Engine's compute logic.

NO WARRANTY
-----------

PLUGINS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. VISENTRIX
IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE OF PLUGINS.

For the full list of what is and is not covered, see LICENSING.md.
